{
  "id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type/rdf_turtle",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "RDF Turtle",
    "es": "RDF Turtle"
  },
  "altLabel": {
    "en": [
      "Terse RDF Triple Language"
    ],
    "es": [
      "Terse RDF Triple Language"
    ]
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Turtle – Terse RDF Triple Language – is a format for expressing data in the Resource Description Framework (RDF) data model with a syntax similar to SPARQL. RDF, in turn, represents information using ‘triples’, each of which consists of a subject, a predicate and an object. Each of those items is expressed as a Web URI.",
    "es": "Turtle – Terse RDF Triple Language – es un formato para expresar datos en el modelo de datos RDF (Resource Description Framework) con una sintaxis similar a SPARQL. RDF, a su vez, representa información usando 'triples', cada uno de los cuales consta de un sujeto, un predicado y un objeto. Cada uno de esos elementos se expresa como una URI Web."
  },
  "notation": [
    ".ttl",
    "text/turtle"
  ],
  "exactMatch": [
    {
      "id": "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/RDF_TURTLE"
